Kreative Studio pose editor (STU-PE1). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Angles are degrees in every API. Coordinates are metres: +X is the figure's left, -Y its front, +Z up. Matrices are arrays of 9 numbers, row-major. Do not change the test file.


Write public/js/pose/depth-parts.js (NAME = depthParts): the mannequin's shapes for the depth picture. Use need('skeleton','./skeleton.js') (S) and need('vec','./vec.js') (V) inside the function. w = fk.solve(pose) = {pos, rot}.

Export primitives(w) only. Write it SHORT (under 60 lines): describe the capsules as data arrays and build them with loops.
primitives(w): a list of {type:'capsule', a:[x,y,z], b:[x,y,z], r} and {type:'ellipsoid', c:[x,y,z], rot: 9-number matrix, radii:[rx,ry,rz]} in world metres. A point q given in rest coordinates and carried by joint j is at at(j, q) = w.pos[j] + w.rot[j] * (q - rest(j)). Parts (from tools/pose-sheet/base_mesh.py):
- head: ellipsoid c = at('head', [0,0,1.68]), rot = w.rot.head, radii [0.088,0.10,0.118]; nose: ellipsoid at('head',[0,-0.105,1.66]), w.rot.head, [0.016,0.02,0.02].
- chest: ellipsoid at('chest',[0,-0.02,1.33]), w.rot.chest, [0.165,0.105,0.17]; waist: at('spine',[0,-0.005,1.13]), w.rot.spine, [0.135,0.09,0.13]; pelvis: at('pelvis',[0,0,0.98]), w.rot.pelvis, [0.155,0.10,0.11].
- neck: capsule w.pos.neck to w.pos.head, r 0.048.
- per side s in l, r: capsule shoulder->elbow r 0.046, elbow->wrist 0.038, hip->knee 0.075, knee->ankle 0.055, ankle->toe 0.04; palm: capsule wrist -> each of thumb_cmc, index_mcp, middle_mcp, ring_mcp, pinky_mcp, r 0.012; fingers: capsule between each consecutive pair of the finger points (thumb_cmc->thumb_mcp->thumb_ip->thumb_tip and the same for index, middle, ring, pinky: mcp->pip->dip->tip), r 0.011 for the thumb, 0.009 for the others.
